        "title": "The Virtual Glass Harmonica",
        "video_ref": "./assets/glass/video.webm",
        "main_txt": "Together with a fellow peer, the design and development of the virtual glass harmonica was a project completed for the <span class='color-glass'>Danish Music Museum</span>. As part of the <i>Music History - Taken out of the Box</i> project, funded by the Augustinus Foundation, it explores the use of <span class='color-glass'>Virtual Reality</span> to resurrect a forgotten instrument and present its history, sound, and interaction through an immersive virtual environment. The installation can be experienced at the Music Museum, where qualitative evaluations have shown that it establishes a good connection between the virtual instrument and the physical 1780-era glass harmonica on display.",
